overrides the primary record.

1040
01:47:59,452 --> 01:48:03,092
In medicine, levels of evidence pyramid is widespread,

1041
01:48:03,712 --> 01:48:07,632
with expert opinions and case reports at the bottom, and cohort and case

1042
01:48:07,692 --> 01:48:11,312
control studies in the middle, randomized trials, and systematic

1043
01:48:11,352 --> 01:48:13,172
reviews and meta-analysis at the top.

1044
01:48:14,232 --> 01:48:17,952
There is a GRADE framework. It rates confidence in a body of evidence as high,

1045
01:48:18,032 --> 01:48:19,112
moderate, low, and very low.

1046
01:48:20,152 --> 01:48:22,992
Explicit separate label not folded in the conclusion.

1047
01:48:23,992 --> 01:48:27,812
And GRADE also decouples evidence quality from recommendation strength.

1048
01:48:28,372 --> 01:48:32,292
A guideline can be a strong recommendation built on low-quality evidence,

1049
01:48:32,472 --> 01:48:34,812
and both facts are stated together, not hidden.

1050
01:48:35,552 --> 01:48:39,312
Medicine has to build this because decisions are

1051
01:48:39,372 --> 01:48:43,072
unavoidable regardless of how imperfect the evidence is, and patient

1052
01:48:43,352 --> 01:48:45,032
needed treatment anyway.

1053
01:48:45,892 --> 01:48:48,212
And biodiversity science and policy

1054
01:48:49,512 --> 01:48:52,812
share a somewhat similar situation with Red List assessments and conservation

1055
01:48:52,872 --> 01:48:54,172
triage and IBBIS reporting,

1056
01:48:56,412 --> 01:48:56,732
all

1057
01:48:58,932 --> 01:49:02,872
contain decisions and conclusions that needs to be drawn from imperfect evidence

1058
01:49:03,092 --> 01:49:04,872
and without long delay.

1059
01:49:06,832 --> 01:49:10,372
So a dataset could carry explicit evidence quality grade

1060
01:49:11,132 --> 01:49:14,492
independent of the decision that is built on top of it.

1061
01:49:19,192 --> 01:49:22,712
Both forensic and archaeological practice separate what was

1062
01:49:22,752 --> 01:49:26,452
recorded from what was concluded and preserve the primary layer

1063
01:49:26,592 --> 01:49:30,152
permanently independent of anyone's interpretation.

1064
01:49:31,692 --> 01:49:35,532
So both fields let multiple competing interpretations coexist linked back

1065
01:49:35,712 --> 01:49:37,112
to the same evidence. And

1066
01:49:38,252 --> 01:49:41,672
we have technical building blocks, identifiers, provenance

1067
01:49:41,712 --> 01:49:42,952
vocabularies, versioning,

1068
01:49:43,752 --> 01:49:44,432
data model.

1069
01:49:46,012 --> 01:49:47,952
And what is missing is

1070
01:49:49,112 --> 01:49:49,312
the

1071
01:49:50,552 --> 01:49:54,432
habit, the routine to treat

1072
01:49:55,112 --> 01:49:58,032
interpretations and detections separately.

1073
01:50:00,332 --> 01:50:04,132
In practical terms, for instance, for identification, we

1074
01:50:04,192 --> 01:50:07,652
started to discuss that it could be useful to

1075
01:50:08,152 --> 01:50:11,292
borrow from, for instance, molecular evidence

1076
